1
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,774
Same cancer, different postcode.

2
00:00:08,074 --> 00:00:11,814
About 65 more lung cancer patients a year would get

3
00:00:11,814 --> 00:00:15,554
curative treatment if every below-average county reached the national rate.

4
00:00:15,854 --> 00:00:19,487
That's Cancer Registry counts for 2019 to

5
00:00:19,487 --> 00:00:23,119
2023. It's illustrative, and it isn't stage-adjusted.

6
00:00:23,419 --> 00:00:25,965
About 12 of them a year are in Lapland.

7
00:00:27,665 --> 00:00:29,201
And it isn't just age.

8
00:00:29,501 --> 00:00:32,719
Age-adjusted, about 16 in 100 men with lung

9
00:00:32,719 --> 00:00:36,742
cancer in Lapland have a curative-treatment record within a year,

10
00:00:36,742 --> 00:00:39,558
against about 30 in 100 in Vantaa-Kerava.

11
00:00:39,858 --> 00:00:43,108
That's a chart estimate from the 2026

12
00:00:43,108 --> 00:00:46,357
Cancer Registry report. The intervals don't overlap.

13
00:00:46,657 --> 00:00:49,562
Women show the same gap. It's not survival.

14
00:00:51,262 --> 00:00:54,434
Goal 3 of Finland's cancer strategy says patients

15
00:00:54,434 --> 00:00:57,209
must start treatment within the target times.

16
00:00:57,509 --> 00:01:01,017
Today no county can see that clock for its own patients.

17
00:01:01,317 --> 00:01:02,732
Tasan is that clock.

18
00:01:04,432 --> 00:01:07,1000
Every lung patient's clock starts when the referral arrives.

19
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,844
On day 28 with no treatment decision,

20
00:01:10,844 --> 00:01:14,479
the nurse navigator gets an alert, and owns that patient.

21
00:01:16,179 --> 00:01:18,702
Every number in Tasan shows its source.

22
00:01:19,002 --> 00:01:23,014
Ask it something nobody in Finland can answer, and it says so.

23
00:01:23,314 --> 00:01:25,251
That missing number is the pilot.

24
00:01:26,951 --> 00:01:30,398
This is what the navigator sees: every open pathway,

25
00:01:30,398 --> 00:01:33,079
sorted by risk, with the blocker named.

26
00:01:33,379 --> 00:01:35,327
These patients are simulated.

27
00:01:37,027 --> 00:01:39,190
To fill the clock from clinical notes,

28
00:01:39,190 --> 00:01:42,590
we ran an open model on a Verda GPU in Finland.

29
00:01:42,890 --> 00:01:44,645
The notes never leave the country,

30
00:01:44,645 --> 00:01:46,986
and the dates go straight into the clock.

31
00:01:48,686 --> 00:01:50,720
Lapland can start on Monday.

32
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:53,998
The chief medical officer signs a 90-day pilot:

33
00:01:53,998 --> 00:01:56,602
one nurse navigator and half an analyst.

34
00:01:56,902 --> 00:02:00,279
In the first month we measure Lapland's own baseline,

35
00:02:00,279 --> 00:02:03,280
and check the registry against the hospital's records.

36
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:06,564
After that, every patient with no treatment decision

37
00:02:06,564 --> 00:02:09,175
by day 28 goes to the navigator.

38
00:02:09,475 --> 00:02:13,472
On day 90, the county decides: go, or stop.

39
00:02:22,572 --> 00:02:27,114
Your challenge asks for a follow-up with a Finnish wellbeing services county.

40
00:02:27,414 --> 00:02:29,859
Our ask: help us put this brief

41
00:02:29,859 --> 00:02:32,305
in front of Lapland's chief medical officer.

42
00:02:32,605 --> 00:02:35,754
Ninety days. One clock. One nurse.

43
00:02:36,054 --> 00:02:39,401
Tasan, koska hoito ei saa riippua postinumerosta.
